.TH "DELETE-OBJECT"  "" "" ""
.SH NAME
delete-object \- 
.SH DESCRIPTION
.sp
Removes an object from a bucket. The behavior depends on the bucket\(aqs versioning state:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
If bucket versioning is not enabled, the operation permanently deletes the object.
.IP \(bu 2
If bucket versioning is enabled, the operation inserts a delete marker, which becomes the current version of the object. To permanently delete an object in a versioned bucket, you must include the object’s \fBversionId\fP in the request. For more information about versioning\-enabled buckets, see \fI\%Deleting object versions from a versioning\-enabled bucket\fP .
.IP \(bu 2
If bucket versioning is suspended, the operation removes the object that has a null \fBversionId\fP , if there is one, and inserts a delete marker that becomes the current version of the object. If there isn\(aqt an object with a null \fBversionId\fP , and all versions of the object have a \fBversionId\fP , Amazon S3 does not remove the object and only inserts a delete marker. To permanently delete an object that has a \fBversionId\fP , you must include the object’s \fBversionId\fP in the request. For more information about versioning\-suspended buckets, see \fI\%Deleting objects from versioning\-suspended buckets\fP .
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDirectory buckets\fP \- S3 Versioning isn\(aqt enabled and supported for directory buckets. For this API operation, only the \fBnull\fP value of the version ID is supported by directory buckets. You can only specify \fBnull\fP to the \fBversionId\fP query parameter in the request.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDirectory buckets\fP \- For directory buckets, you must make requests for this API operation to the Zonal endpoint. These endpoints support virtual\-hosted\-style requests in the format 
.nf
\(ga\(ga
.fi
\fI\%https://\fP\fIamzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket\fP .s3express\-\fIzone\-id\fP .*region\-code* .amazonaws.com/\fIkey\-name\fP \(ga\(ga . Path\-style requests are not supported. For more information about endpoints in Availability Zones, see \fI\%Regional and Zonal endpoints for directory buckets in Availability Zones\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP . For more information about endpoints in Local Zones, see \fI\%Concepts for directory buckets in Local Zones\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.IP "System Message: WARNING/2 (<string>:, line 39)"
Inline literal start\-string without end\-string.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
To remove a specific version, you must use the \fBversionId\fP query parameter. Using this query parameter permanently deletes the version. If the object deleted is a delete marker, Amazon S3 sets the response header \fBx\-amz\-delete\-marker\fP to true.
.sp
If the object you want to delete is in a bucket where the bucket versioning configuration is MFA Delete enabled, you must include the \fBx\-amz\-mfa\fP request header in the DELETE \fBversionId\fP request. Requests that include \fBx\-amz\-mfa\fP must use HTTPS. For more information about MFA Delete, see \fI\%Using MFA Delete\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP . To see sample requests that use versioning, see \fI\%Sample Request\fP .
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBDirectory buckets\fP \- MFA delete is not supported by directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
You can delete objects by explicitly calling DELETE Object or calling (\fI\%PutBucketLifecycle\fP ) to enable Amazon S3 to remove them for you. If you want to block users or accounts from removing or deleting objects from your bucket, you must deny them the \fBs3:DeleteObject\fP , \fBs3:DeleteObjectVersion\fP , and \fBs3:PutLifeCycleConfiguration\fP actions.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBDirectory buckets\fP \- S3 Lifecycle is not supported by directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Permissions
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBGeneral purpose bucket permissions\fP \- The following permissions are required in your policies when your \fBDeleteObjects\fP request includes specific headers.
.INDENT 2.0
.IP \(bu 2

.nf
**
.fi
\fBs3:DeleteObject\fP ** \- To delete an object from a bucket, you must always have the \fBs3:DeleteObject\fP permission.
.IP "System Message: WARNING/2 (<string>:, line 82)"
Inline strong start\-string without end\-string.
.IP \(bu 2

.nf
**
.fi
\fBs3:DeleteObjectVersion\fP ** \- To delete a specific version of an object from a versioning\-enabled bucket, you must have the \fBs3:DeleteObjectVersion\fP permission.
.IP "System Message: WARNING/2 (<string>:, line 84)"
Inline strong start\-string without end\-string.
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDirectory bucket permissions\fP \- To grant access to this API operation on a directory bucket, we recommend that you use the \(ga \fBCreateSession\fP \fI\%https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/API/API_CreateSession\fP\&.html\(ga__ API operation for session\-based authorization. Specifically, you grant the \fBs3express:CreateSession\fP permission to the directory bucket in a bucket policy or an IAM identity\-based policy. Then, you make the \fBCreateSession\fP API call on the bucket to obtain a session token. With the session token in your request header, you can make API requests to this operation. After the session token expires, you make another \fBCreateSession\fP API call to generate a new session token for use. Amazon Web Services CLI or SDKs create session and refresh the session token automatically to avoid service interruptions when a session expires. For more information about authorization, see \(ga \fBCreateSession\fP \fI\%https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/API/API_CreateSession\fP\&.html\(ga__ .
.sp
HTTP Host header syntax
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBDirectory buckets\fP \- The HTTP Host header syntax is \(ga\(ga \fIBucket\-name\fP .s3express\-\fIzone\-id\fP .*region\-code* .amazonaws.com\(ga\(ga .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The following action is related to \fBDeleteObject\fP :
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%PutObject\fP
.UNINDENT
.sp
See also: AWS API Documentation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
  delete\-object
\-\-bucket <value>
\-\-key <value>
[\-\-mfa <value>]
[\-\-version\-id <value>]
[\-\-request\-payer <value>]
[\-\-bypass\-governance\-retention | \-\-no\-bypass\-governance\-retention]
[\-\-expected\-bucket\-owner <value>]
[\-\-if\-match <value>]
[\-\-if\-match\-last\-modified\-time <value>]
[\-\-if\-match\-size <value>]
[\-\-cli\-input\-json | \-\-cli\-input\-yaml]
[\-\-generate\-cli\-skeleton <value>]
[\-\-debug]
[\-\-endpoint\-url <value>]
[\-\-no\-verify\-ssl]
[\-\-no\-paginate]
[\-\-output <value>]
[\-\-query <value>]
[\-\-profile <value>]
[\-\-region <value>]
[\-\-version <value>]
[\-\-color <value>]
[\-\-no\-sign\-request]
[\-\-ca\-bundle <value>]
[\-\-cli\-read\-timeout <value>]
[\-\-cli\-connect\-timeout <value>]
[\-\-cli\-binary\-format <value>]
[\-\-no\-cli\-pager]
[\-\-cli\-auto\-prompt]
[\-\-no\-cli\-auto\-prompt]
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH OPTIONS
.sp
\fB\-\-bucket\fP (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The bucket name of the bucket containing the object.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBDirectory buckets\fP \- When you use this operation with a directory bucket, you must use virtual\-hosted\-style requests in the format \(ga\(ga \fIBucket\-name\fP .s3express\-\fIzone\-id\fP .*region\-code* .amazonaws.com\(ga\(ga . Path\-style requests are not supported. Directory bucket names must be unique in the chosen Zone (Availability Zone or Local Zone). Bucket names must follow the format \(ga\(ga \fIbucket\-base\-name\fP \-\-\fIzone\-id\fP \-\-x\-s3\(ga\(ga (for example, \(ga\(ga \fIamzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket\fP \-\-\fIusw2\-az1\fP \-\-x\-s3\(ga\(ga ). For information about bucket naming restrictions, see \fI\%Directory bucket naming rules\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.sp
\fBAccess points\fP \- When you use this action with an access point for general purpose buckets, you must provide the alias of the access point in place of the bucket name or specify the access point ARN. When you use this action with an access point for directory buckets, you must provide the access point name in place of the bucket name. When using the access point ARN, you must direct requests to the access point hostname. The access point hostname takes the form \fIAccessPointName\fP \-\fIAccountId\fP .s3\-accesspoint.*Region* .amazonaws.com. When using this action with an access point through the Amazon Web Services SDKs, you provide the access point ARN in place of the bucket name. For more information about access point ARNs, see \fI\%Using access points\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Object Lambda access points are not supported by directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBS3 on Outposts\fP \- When you use this action with S3 on Outposts, you must direct requests to the S3 on Outposts hostname. The S3 on Outposts hostname takes the form \(ga\(ga \fIAccessPointName\fP \-\fIAccountId\fP .*outpostID* .s3\-outposts.*Region* .amazonaws.com\(ga\(ga . When you use this action with S3 on Outposts, the destination bucket must be the Outposts access point ARN or the access point alias. For more information about S3 on Outposts, see \fI\%What is S3 on Outposts?\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-key\fP (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Key name of the object to delete.
.sp
Constraints:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
min: \fB1\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-mfa\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The concatenation of the authentication device\(aqs serial number, a space, and the value that is displayed on your authentication device. Required to permanently delete a versioned object if versioning is configured with MFA delete enabled.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-version\-id\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Version ID used to reference a specific version of the object.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
For directory buckets in this API operation, only the \fBnull\fP value of the version ID is supported.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-request\-payer\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Confirms that the requester knows that they will be charged for the request. Bucket owners need not specify this parameter in their requests. If either the source or destination S3 bucket has Requester Pays enabled, the requester will pay for corresponding charges to copy the object. For information about downloading objects from Requester Pays buckets, see \fI\%Downloading Objects in Requester Pays Buckets\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBrequester\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-bypass\-governance\-retention\fP | \fB\-\-no\-bypass\-governance\-retention\fP (boolean)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Indicates whether S3 Object Lock should bypass Governance\-mode restrictions to process this operation. To use this header, you must have the \fBs3:BypassGovernanceRetention\fP permission.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-expected\-bucket\-owner\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The account ID of the expected bucket owner. If the account ID that you provide does not match the actual owner of the bucket, the request fails with the HTTP status code \fB403 Forbidden\fP (access denied).
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-if\-match\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The \fBIf\-Match\fP header field makes the request method conditional on ETags. If the ETag value does not match, the operation returns a \fB412 Precondition Failed\fP error. If the ETag matches or if the object doesn\(aqt exist, the operation will return a \fB204 Success (No Content) response\fP .
.sp
For more information about conditional requests, see \fI\%RFC 7232\fP .
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is only supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-if\-match\-last\-modified\-time\fP (timestamp)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
If present, the object is deleted only if its modification times matches the provided \fBTimestamp\fP . If the \fBTimestamp\fP values do not match, the operation returns a \fB412 Precondition Failed\fP error. If the \fBTimestamp\fP matches or if the object doesn’t exist, the operation returns a \fB204 Success (No Content)\fP response.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is only supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-if\-match\-size\fP (long)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
If present, the object is deleted only if its size matches the provided size in bytes. If the \fBSize\fP value does not match, the operation returns a \fB412 Precondition Failed\fP error. If the \fBSize\fP matches or if the object doesn’t exist, the operation returns a \fB204 Success (No Content)\fP response.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is only supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBWARNING:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
You can use the \fBIf\-Match\fP , \fBx\-amz\-if\-match\-last\-modified\-time\fP and \fBx\-amz\-if\-match\-size\fP conditional headers in conjunction with each\-other or individually.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-input\-json\fP | \fB\-\-cli\-input\-yaml\fP (string)
Reads arguments from the JSON string provided. The JSON string follows the format provided by \fB\-\-generate\-cli\-skeleton\fP\&. If other arguments are provided on the command line, those values will override the JSON\-provided values. It is not possible to pass arbitrary binary values using a JSON\-provided value as the string will be taken literally. This may not be specified along with \fB\-\-cli\-input\-yaml\fP\&.
.sp
\fB\-\-generate\-cli\-skeleton\fP (string)
Prints a JSON skeleton to standard output without sending an API request. If provided with no value or the value \fBinput\fP, prints a sample input JSON that can be used as an argument for \fB\-\-cli\-input\-json\fP\&. Similarly, if provided \fByaml\-input\fP it will print a sample input YAML that can be used with \fB\-\-cli\-input\-yaml\fP\&. If provided with the value \fBoutput\fP, it validates the command inputs and returns a sample output JSON for that command. The generated JSON skeleton is not stable between versions of the AWS CLI and there are no backwards compatibility guarantees in the JSON skeleton generated.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.sp
\fB\-\-debug\fP (boolean)
.sp
Turn on debug logging.
.sp
\fB\-\-endpoint\-url\fP (string)
.sp
Override command\(aqs default URL with the given URL.
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-verify\-ssl\fP (boolean)
.sp
By default, the AWS CLI uses SSL when communicating with AWS services. For each SSL connection, the AWS CLI will verify SSL certificates. This option overrides the default behavior of verifying SSL certificates.
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-paginate\fP (boolean)
.sp
Disable automatic pagination. If automatic pagination is disabled, the AWS CLI will only make one call, for the first page of results.
.sp
\fB\-\-output\fP (string)
.sp
The formatting style for command output.
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
text
.IP \(bu 2
table
.IP \(bu 2
yaml
.IP \(bu 2
yaml\-stream
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-query\fP (string)
.sp
A JMESPath query to use in filtering the response data.
.sp
\fB\-\-profile\fP (string)
.sp
Use a specific profile from your credential file.
.sp
\fB\-\-region\fP (string)
.sp
The region to use. Overrides config/env settings.
.sp
\fB\-\-version\fP (string)
.sp
Display the version of this tool.
.sp
\fB\-\-color\fP (string)
.sp
Turn on/off color output.
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-sign\-request\fP (boolean)
.sp
Do not sign requests. Credentials will not be loaded if this argument is provided.
.sp
\fB\-\-ca\-bundle\fP (string)
.sp
The CA certificate bundle to use when verifying SSL certificates. Overrides config/env settings.
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-read\-timeout\fP (int)
.sp
The maximum socket read time in seconds. If the value is set to 0, the socket read will be blocking and not timeout. The default value is 60 seconds.
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-connect\-timeout\fP (int)
.sp
The maximum socket connect time in seconds. If the value is set to 0, the socket connect will be blocking and not timeout. The default value is 60 seconds.
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-binary\-format\fP (string)
.sp
The formatting style to be used for binary blobs. The default format is base64. The base64 format expects binary blobs to be provided as a base64 encoded string. The raw\-in\-base64\-out format preserves compatibility with AWS CLI V1 behavior and binary values must be passed literally. When providing contents from a file that map to a binary blob \fBfileb://\fP will always be treated as binary and use the file contents directly regardless of the \fBcli\-binary\-format\fP setting. When using \fBfile://\fP the file contents will need to properly formatted for the configured \fBcli\-binary\-format\fP\&.
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
base64
.IP \(bu 2
raw\-in\-base64\-out
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-cli\-pager\fP (boolean)
.sp
Disable cli pager for output.
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-auto\-prompt\fP (boolean)
.sp
Automatically prompt for CLI input parameters.
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-cli\-auto\-prompt\fP (boolean)
.sp
Disable automatically prompt for CLI input parameters.
.SH EXAMPLES
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
To use the following examples, you must have the AWS CLI installed and configured. See the \fI\%Getting started guide\fP in the \fIAWS CLI User Guide\fP for more information.
.sp
Unless otherwise stated, all examples have unix\-like quotation rules. These examples will need to be adapted to your terminal\(aqs quoting rules. See \fI\%Using quotation marks with strings\fP in the \fIAWS CLI User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The following command deletes an object named \fBtest.txt\fP from a bucket named \fBamzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
aws s3api delete\-object \-\-bucket amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket \-\-key test.txt
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If bucket versioning is enabled, the output will contain the version ID of the delete marker:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
{
  \(dqVersionId\(dq: \(dq9_gKg5vG56F.TTEUdwkxGpJ3tNDlWlGq\(dq,
  \(dqDeleteMarker\(dq: true
}
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
For more information about deleting objects, see \fI\%Deleting Objects\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 Developer Guide\fP\&.
.SH OUTPUT
.sp
DeleteMarker \-> (boolean)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Indicates whether the specified object version that was permanently deleted was (true) or was not (false) a delete marker before deletion. In a simple DELETE, this header indicates whether (true) or not (false) the current version of the object is a delete marker. To learn more about delete markers, see \fI\%Working with delete markers\fP .
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
VersionId \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Returns the version ID of the delete marker created as a result of the DELETE operation.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
RequestCharged \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
If present, indicates that the requester was successfully charged for the request. For more information, see \fI\%Using Requester Pays buckets for storage transfers and usage\fP in the \fIAmazon Simple Storage Service user guide\fP .
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBrequester\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
